<%#
  Inline validation message for a single attribute — the first error only.

  Lifted verbatim from account/profile, which was the only form in the app that
  actually told the user what went wrong. boards/new and boards/edit relied on
  Rails' field_with_errors wrapper instead, and this app has no CSS for that
  wrapper at all, so a rejected board name produced no visible feedback of any
  kind. Three call sites is enough to share rather than triplicate.

  Deliberately scoped to ONE attribute rather than dumping full_messages: every
  call site renders this directly beneath the field it belongs to, so the
  attribute name would be redundant in the text ("can't be blank" sits under the
  Name label).

  Renders nothing at all when the attribute has no errors, so it's safe to place
  unconditionally.

  locals: record (an ActiveModel), attribute (Symbol)
%>
<% if record.errors[attribute].any? %>
  <p class="text-xs text-danger-600"><%= record.errors[attribute].first %></p>
<% end %>
